#1  Cognitive bias
===============================================================================================

  In a universe governed by ubiquitous and permanent causality, everything relies on everything
  across the whole infinity of the space-time continuum.

  Does "proportional to its own rate of change" relate to anything known?
  Is "whole infinty" more paradoxical than  exp (x) = 0 ?

  Many phenomena evolve across space-time with an exponential curve.
  Yet we often perceive them as linear.

  Which means that our brain constantly performs a mathematical transform:
  the reciprocal to exponentiation -- logarithms.

  Of course this is just a convention.
  Everything is exponential because we assume space-time is linear.
  Maybe space-time is logarithmic and everything is linear...

  Maybe  E = m + 2c ?

  Maybe the Big Bang is not a moment? Maybe it's an asymptote?

  Only a point of view, a referential. Choose your favourite maths.
